.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt VIFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vifs
.Nd edit the file system table safely
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
edits
.Pa /etc/fstab .
It locks the file, so that two
.Nm
cannot edit it at once, and opens a copy of it in the editor named by
.Ev EDITOR ,
or
.Xr vi 1 .
When the editor ends, the copy replaces
.Pa /etc/fstab
in one step, and only if it was changed; if the editor fails, the file is
left as it was.
.Pp
.Pa /etc/fstab
is created if it does not exist.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width EDITOR
.It Ev EDITOR
The editor to run, through
.Xr sh 1 ,
with the copy's name after it.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/fstab -compact
.It Pa /etc/fstab
the file system table
.It Pa /etc/vifs.XXXXXX
the copy being edited
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr vipw 8
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
